WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.960
*Spooky music*

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.180
*Fi Fai fo Fum*

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.180
*...*

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.560
*Screams*

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.360
*I smell Diet Coke....*

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.260
*Spooky music again*

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.320
*Hmmm!*

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.020
*Yummy...*

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:22.320
*Screams*

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.140
*Screams*

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.320
*Fade to black, dramatic music aaand title card*

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.260
Hello internet!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.260
Welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.320
The Kaiju monster

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.160
Of smart internet shows.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.020
*Matzilla scream*

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.400
Wait, does that even make sense?

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.820
An over-sized internet show about...

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.320
I don't know,

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.120
I guess it sounded good in my head,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.320
but now, just saying it out loud

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.760
I just sound stupid...

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.380
And also, now that i think of, it'd

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.040
be redundant since Kaiju implies

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.040
the monster half, so...I don't know,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:48.960
now I'm all screwed up.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.180
ANYWAY!

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.820
When it comes to over-sized Kaiju monsters!--

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.440
double redundancy there!

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.540
No one beats...

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.420
Gamera~!

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.800
Kids; Gamera! Gamera!

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.880
Gamera!!! * HOLY CRAP TURTLE BACKFLIPZ OMG!!11 *

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.220
I don't care who you are!

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.780
You can't beat a rocket-powered, flying turtle monster! (Well, everyone knows that.)

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.100
But the most famous of the Kaiju, *Bye Gamera!*

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.920
are the two big ol' classics themselves...

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.660
Godzilla and King Kong.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:14.000
Over the years, these two enormous monsters have had dozens of movies made about them.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.480
I'm sure most of you are already familiar with Godzilla's backstory.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:21.300
He's a prehistoric sea monster awakened by nuclear radiation

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.440
but King Kong's backstory-- well, that's a bit more mysterious,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.900
or, at least it was...Until today!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.740
because I did the research, and by looking closely at the new movie "Kong: Skull Island,"

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.120
past King Kong lore, and good old-fashioned science,

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.700
we can start to piece together the big ape's origin, and not ONLY that

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.240
but also some of the hidden secrets that I predict you'll be seeing revealed

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:48.600
over the next few movies in this kaiju monster universe that's been kicked off by "Godzilla" and "Skull Island."

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.020
Ready to go?  Cue that ominous stinger!

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.400
*Ominous music much?*

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.880
Previously, the only thing we knew for certain about Kong was his home, Skull Island

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.840
In the original 1930's classic,

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.920
this island was geographically located 12 degrees south and 78 degrees east on the map.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.360
The closest real-life island to these coordinates is the Cocos Island,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.820
otherwise known as the Keeling Island.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.600
And if you compare the Keeling Island to Skull Island,

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.840
they're pretty much an exact match--

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.780
a coral atoll teeming with overgrown vegetables and a tropical monsoon climate.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.640
I mean, the only REAL difference between the two is that one's renowned for its beautiful beaches

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.520
and the other has prehistoric dragon creatures and a giant ape.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.260
So... pretty much the exact same.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:30.760
*Camera flash, ukulele music, cheerings from Cocos Island!*

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.060
And that was all we had for decades.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:37.000
Now fast-forward to 2004 and the release of Peter Jackson's "King Kong" remake.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.300
In a tie-in novel released alongside the movie,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.720
it's revealed that Kong and the other prehistoric creatures on Skull Island

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.600
survived due to its isolated location.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.600
But is that even possible?

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.400
Could some large monsters from prehistoric times have survived thousands of years

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:55.920
past that ancient extinction asteroid that killed off the dinosaurs

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.460
and be hiding out in some remote island today?

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.560
Well, yes!  And no.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.340
You see, there are quite a few Jurassic-age species that survived the K-T Extinction Event,

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.320
or the Cretaceous-Tertiary Extinction Event.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.060
That's the fancy, scientific name for the events that killed off the dinosaurs.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:14.100
And when I say quite a few, I mean a bunch!

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:18.480
I mean, we all think of that asteroid hitting the earth as an event that killed off EVERYTHING,

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.480
but in reality, almost 84% of marine life made it:

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:26.680
crocodiles, certain types of fish, frogs, even a few, small land mammals.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.960
Don't believe the lies your third-grade science teacher is peddlin'!

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:31.580
*Matpat Falcon Punches your third-grade lying teacher*

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.220
But there is a key word here, and that word is small.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:39.820
After the asteroid's impact with earth, the theory goes that the atmosphere changed drastically.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:44.380
So some smaller species survived, but larger species--BOOM!

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.760
Completely wiped out.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.340
Thus, dinosaurs=extinct.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:53.320
But there is one way dinosaurs actually could have survived, and that's underground.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.980
In 2007, scientists discovered an underground den of dinosaur bones,

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:01.360
suggesting that some dinosaurs survived that initial K-T extinction

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.720
by avoiding the extreme changes in the environment

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:07.640
in the only place that was safe--inside the earth.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.060
And we see that the new movie "Kong: Skull Island" actually backs that theory up.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.660
Houston Brooks (ding!) one of the Monarch scientists on the hunt for the kaiju,

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.340
name-drops the Hollow Earth Theory.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:24.000
This theory claims that within the earth, there are hollow interior spaces that have their own magnetic poles and atmospheres.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.060
Per Brooks, the dinosaurs must have gone into these hollow spaces,

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.700
surviving well-past the K-T event, to the 1970s when the movie begins,

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:37.440
which, scientifically speaking, in the real world is incredibly far-fetched,

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:41.120
but in the Kong-verse, it's entirely possible and looks to be true!

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.940
Thus, we have the origins of the underground Skull-Crawlers,

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:47.000
and in a brilliant design detail on the part of the movie's designers,

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.420
you can tell that the Skull-Crawlers adapted to a life spent burrowed within the earth.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.020
They have sunken eyes and skeletal features.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.180
It's awesome to see that level of detail!

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:00.460
But NONE of this explains Kong.  He's still as hairy and muscular as ever,

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.640
showing no signs of his species having to adapt to living in caves for millions of years.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:07.000
There's . . . something else going on here.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.480
So if Kong wasn't Netflix and chilling since prehistoric times, then where did he come from?

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.380
To figure this out, we need to trace Kong's family history.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:18.220
The closest ancient ancestors to Kong are the Giganthopithecus Blacki,

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.580
a species of ape that existed from 9 million  to one hundred thousand years ago.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:28.240
These apes, originating from South China and Vietnam, were the biggest apes that ever walked the earth,

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.500
standing at a whopping ten feet tall!

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:36.340
But, obviously, even at ten feet tall, Kong dwarfs these giant apes.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.100
According to "Kong: Skull Island's" director, quote,

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.660
So that places him nearly ten times the height of the Giganthopithecus,

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.320
and while I admit that may seem initially like a theory killer,

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.940
a recent study published in the 2015 "Journal of Science" tracked the relationship between

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:02.840
the sizes of large animals and time.  According to their study, it took 542 million years

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.300
for marine animals to increase in size by 150-fold.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.920
Comparing this statistical growth to the  Giganthopithecus Blacki's 9 million year history,

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.680
the average size could, theoretically, increase by . . .

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:21.100
150 divided by 542 million equals x over 9 million, cross-multiply, divide and separate out the X and (drum roll)--

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:24.100
APPROXIMATELY 2.5 TIMES!

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.620
Uh . . . yeah.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:30.600
So at most, it would be, like, twenty feet, not the hundred-foot mammoth that we end up seeing, so . . .

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.340
Yeah, that one ended up being a theory killer. (shattering sound) But hey, you know what, that's OK

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.280
because there'd still be one fatal flaw.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:41.820
In "Kong: Skull Island," the downed World War II pilot Hank Marlow reveals that the local tribes on the island

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:46.380
had to survive thousands of years against the Skull-Crawlers without any help from Kong.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:52.100
Then suddenly, out of nowhere, the Kongs appeared and fought back against the Skull-Crawlers, protecting the tribe members.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:55.380
But . . . that's a weird detail right?

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.600
Giant apes don't just pop into existence.  They gotta come from somewhere.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:04.100
It's almost like Kong was placed on the island rather than grew up there,

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.280
and THAT'S exactly what happened.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:10.440
If you pay close attention to the new movie, there's a blink-and-you'll miss it cameo by a familiar name

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.160
that gives this whole conspiracy away.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.100
When Marlow reveals the island's history to the group of survivors,

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:20.660
they're in a temple the natives built to worship Kong, and where's that temple located?

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:26.220
Inside of a ship.  But why would the natives ever build their temple in the decrepit bowels of a ship

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.940
instead of, say, a cave, or something?

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:34.300
Well, as the characters enter into the ship-temple, for a few seconds we see the ship's name--

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:40.440
Now, for those of you who are unfamiliar, the Wanderer is the name of the ship from the 1930's film,

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:44.840
the ship that transported King Kong from Skull Island to New York,

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:49.700
but in this new reboot, the Wanderer isn't rusting on the docks of New York but instead

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.120
it's rusting away on Skull Island.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:56.560
This new reboot has deliberately inverted the boat's whereabouts,

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.960
suggesting that Kong wasn't brought from Skull Island to New York, as it's always been,

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.560
but instead was brought from New York to Skull Island.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:10.220
The locals have created an altar for Kong in the ship that delivered their savior to them.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:15.220
Now, before you call me bananas, remember that the most important thing about this new version of "King Kong"

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.240
and the thing that separates it out from all previous versions,

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:21.720
is that it's a part of a shared universe with Godzilla--

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:24.340
because everyone wants to be Marvel these days--

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:26.460
and in the 2014 "Godzilla" movie,

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:32.860
we actually learn the U. S. government already knows about the existence of kaiju as early as 1850.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:37.060
In fact, the kaiju are such a threat that the U. S. government forms MONARCH,

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:40.780
a secret organization to hunt and study these giant monsters

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:45.240
MONARCH even lures Godzilla to an island where they detonate a nuke to kill it.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:51.160
Of course, this nuke has the opposite effect.  Godzilla actually gets stronger with each dose of radiation.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.920
So, facing monsters that take their greatest weapon of the atom bomb

00:08:54.920 --> 00:09:01.840
and treat it like a shot of Power Thirst, what could MONARCH possibly do  other than create their own monster?

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:05.760
And that's not just me spit-balling; just look at the company name itself.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:10.880
In the real world, Monarch is a real company, a company that, according to their website,

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:15.720
collects information on genes and mutations for biomedical research.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.560
And if you think it's just a coincidence that the fictional MONARCH government agency

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:24.020
and this real scientific institution just so happened to share the same name,

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:30.020
look no further than their logos.  They're almost exactly alike--two sideways infinity symbols.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:34.660
What I'm saying is that in the movies King isn't just some random prehistoric ape.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:38.680
The science and timelines just don't add up, but you know what does?

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:45.140
Gene mutations done by MONARCH.  I mean, scientists are already using gene mutation to increase the size of animals

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:52.140
Researchers at the Salk Institute created genetically stronger and larger mice by suppressing specific genes,

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:57.200
and genetically modified salmon are programmed to grow year-round instead of just during spring and summer.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:04.360
After just eighteen months, these salmon were almost double the length and three times the weight of a normal salmon.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:09.920
So it's not that far of a stretch to say that a fictional government organization named after a REAL organization

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:16.080
that specializes in gene science would use this exact same tech to craft genetically larger apes.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:23.320
As we learn in "Skull Island," per Marlow, King Kong's only just a kid, which doesn't actually make sense on paper.

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:29.280
Given that the lifespan of a typical ape is forty years, and Marlow's only been stuck on the island for twenty-six,

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:34.700
Kong should be pushing middle-age, and yet King Kong is "still only a kid"?

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.700
Why?  Well, because of genetic modification.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.400
During puberty in animals, there's an increased production of the hormone estrogen.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:46.220
The high-concentration of estrogen in the blood causes growth plates in the bones to fuse

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:51.960
thus closing down growth centers of bones and preventing my pimply-sixteen-year-old self from getting taller.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:56.820
However, if you manipulated TeenPat's genes to reduce the production of estrogen during puberty,

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:01.180
then the size of my nerdy, Dockers-wearing self would increase without limit.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:07.280
I would finally become the tall, masculine god that I have always envisioned myself to be!

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:13.160
The same applies to Kong!  If MONARCH had altered the ape's genetic makeup to keep him growing,

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:19.540
what they essentially did was delay his puberty, keeping him, as Marlow says, "only a kid."

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:24.440
So then, what is the true lineage of King Kong?  Well, lemme break it down for ya.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:29.540
In the 1850s, scientists discovered the existence of kaiju-life living within the earth's surface.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:35.140
They try everything to defeat these monsters--bombs, nukes, radiation poisoning--but nothing works.

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:41.360
Faced with an unprecedented threat, they decide to fight fire with fire, creating their own genetically-modified creatures--

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:46.200
super-large apes.  After creating these apes, they ship them off to an isolated island,

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:50.120
an island, per their research, that may be a hot-spot for kaiju life.

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:54.840
They wait for over sixty years for their apes to grow and evolve on that island,

00:11:54.840 --> 00:12:00.100
but in the 1970's, as their money and influence dwindles, MONARCH has no choice but to prove to the government

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:06.700
that their research wasn't for naught.  (crash sound) They send two scientists armed with a couple of bombs and a camera on a trip to Skull Island

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:11.360
to document the fruits of their labor.  Once over the island, these scientists drop bombs,

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:17.140
awakening the kaiju's dwelling beneath the earth's surface, all to see if their monster, King Kong,

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:23.000
has what it takes to defeat them.  The whole trip to Skull Island in the new Kong movie is nothing more than a test-run

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:30.560
to see if MONACH's masterpiece, King Kong, has what it takes to defeat humanity's greatest threat--Godzilla.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:38.820
It's just gonna take until 2020 and the whole connected, kaiju universe to see these two skyscraper-sized monsters finally cross paths!

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:45.100
But hey, that's just a theory--a Film Theory!

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.700
Aaaaaaaand cut!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:50.020
Remember a few weeks ago when I did that episode on "The Walking Dead,"

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:55.220
talking about how the series is all touchy-feely, got to interview Robert Kirkman the creator of the series

00:12:55.220 --> 00:13:01.500
to talk to him about theories, both the good (like secret clues hidden in Tyreese's death) and the bad (like the coma theories)?

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:02.280
"You heard it here--"

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.500
"That would be the worst."

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.000
"Stop it with the coma!"

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.680
Well, he and his team enjoyed the interview and the episode SO MUCH

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:11.780
that they put me as a character in their video game--

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.600
How cool is that?!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:18.020
Apparently, I'm a savior and armed (gun cocking sound) to the max!

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.780
So if you ever wanted to team up with me,

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:24.460
or feed me to a hoard of hungry zombies eager to tear out my throat with their teeth

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:27.800
then download "Walking Dead: Road to Survival," and when you find me,

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:33.580
take a screenshot and send it on in!  I would love to see you guys mutilate my twitching undead corpse.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:39.100
And hey, a very, very special thank you to the Walking Dead and their gaming team Scopley

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:41.440
for partnering with me to make that happen.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:44.680
Get slaughtering, my friends!  I'll leave a link in the description.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:51.520
I am so excited about this opportunity, and I am so excited to share it with you guys.  So go out there, find me, and enjoy the game!

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:57.920
It's free to download, so really there's no excuse outside of "I don't have a phone," in which case that's a perfectly valid excuse.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.680
But otherwise, find me and kill me.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:05.200
Now if you'll excuse me, I gotta prep for next week, and I believe the seas are calling my name.

